 polls could pull the race back toward a single-digit tossup.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Open seat: Gretchen Whitmer (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Michigan's governorship is open as Gretchen Whitmer is term-limited, and Democrats have nominated Secretary of State Jocelyn Benson against Republican John James, a two-time congressional and Senate candidate. The race has drawn heavy attention in a state with an even partisan lean, but Benson has led consistently throughout the fall.\n\nEvery poll since early October shows Benson ahead, with recent surveys from Marist, SSRS, and Mitchell putting her lead between 5 and 12 points. She has also outraised James substantially and holds a large cash advantage. Expert ratings cluster at Lean D with several Likely D calls, and prediction markets give her roughly a 92-94% chance. James has campaigned on change and accountability, but the polling trend has moved toward Benson rather than away from her in the final stretch.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9339, "margin": 7.39}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9166, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9224, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9193, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.8901, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9053, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.911, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9221, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9131, "margin": 6.8}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9322, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.912, "margin": 6.8}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9194, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9194, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.8925, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9071, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9049, "margin": 6.8}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.8998, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.8901, "